ent": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The total is 5 \u00d7 $189 (DK-200) + 5 \u00d7 $529 (MN-32) = $3,590. That's over $2,500, so the order needs manager approval. I'll submit it through the primary supplier so it can go to the approver.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01K9EJT64gFqSx3yceEPDW4x", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"lines": [{"sku": "DK-200", "qty": 5}, {"sku": "MN-32", "qty": 5}], "ship_to": "HQ", "idempotency_key": "design-hires-dk200-mn32-x5-hq", "confidence": 0.85}, "name": "place_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I placed purchase order PO0001 for the new design hires, but it went through without a manager approval step, even though our policy requires one for orders over $2,500.\n\n**Order details**\n- **Order ID:** PO0001 (primary supplier)\n- **Status:** Placed\n- **Ship to:** HQ\n- **Items:**\n  - 5 \u00d7 USB-C Dock DK-200 (new) at $189 each = $945\n  - 5 \u00d7 32-inch 5K Monitor MN-32 (new) at $529 each = $2,645\n- **Total:** $3,590\n\nDK-200 was in stock, so I didn't need the DK-210. I skipped the cheaper refurbished DK-200-R since you asked for new equipment only.\n\n**About the approval:** I expected the order to be sent to the manager for sign-off first. Instead it came back as \"placed\" straight away, so it doesn't seem to have been sent to them. Please check with the manager. If they don't approve it, I can cancel PO0001 and get a refund.", "type": "text"}]}]}